  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2025-12-04T02:42:42.695Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "I've been wanting to be able to move the location in which I hear audio from on avatars.\n\nFor example, some of my avatars have ears on top of their heads or somewhere else besides the human placement. \n\nIf I am wearing an avatar with ears on the top, like a fox or cat, I would like to be able to hear from the avatar's ears instead of where my viewpoint is.\n\nIt would be even cooler if we could dedicate specific locations on the body for either the left or right audio (if that's even technically possible). Perhaps just being able to move it around like the viewpoint ball can already do.\n\n- Perhaps maybe a toggle settings as well, for those who like the avatar, but would like to hear like normal. This way the avatar doesn't feel too uncomfortable for the users if the uploaders have this feature enabled.\n\nFor security sake,\n\nI think that only being able to move them around a certain distance from the head would be perfect, so that that players wouldn't be able to abuse the distance to spy on other players in a world. \n\nI believe this would be a great way to be more immersed with the avatar people are wearing.",
